  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tina
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Tina
  LastName: Meskhi
  Nickname: 
  Occupation: Accountant
  CharacterDescription: Controlled, seductive, and carefully evasive. She wears a porcelain mask at all times, claiming it covers old scars -- though she volunteers this explanation so readily it feels rehearsed. An accountant with no recorded family and no traceable past. She deploys warmth and charm deliberately, and if you press her with too many questions, she will offer you something other than answers.
  CharacterArc: Her arc traces a woman who has always worked behind two masks -- the literal porcelain one on her face, and the persona of harmless performer she uses as cover. As the crisis deepens and checkpoints grow harder to pass, her attempts to bribe shift from casual to desperate. In the end, the question of what the mask actually hides -- scars, identity, or something else entirely -- becomes the one thing she cannot charm her way past.
  DateOfBirth: 01/01/1966
  Sex: Female
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 02 DEC
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f8e89ead54f8523428cc2e34f005bb5e, type: 2}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: {x: 4, y: 10}
  alterEgoName: 
  basePersonalityDescriptors: []
  normalBehaviorNotes: Seductive and flirtatious by default. Deflects personal questions with charm. Will attempt to bribe the inspector if questioned too heavily. Claims the mask covers old scars but never elaborates. No family recorded -- appears deliberate.
  fullMutantDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ed8202744667b844895a3eba3cf0674f, type: 2}
  replacementIDPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: b95f411c45eb9a24c86202f9a0008a9f, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 1501177916931924578, guid: 572c6160c8045c14eb3dd93c39663819, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Client meeting, downtown finance office.
    - Home after late-night bookkeeping.
    - Delivering ledgers to the treasury district.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Collecting payments from an associate.
    - Meeting clients I won't name.
    - Checking secured deposits. Things deteriorate.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Closing accounts before the last deadline.
    - Final settlement papers for a client.
    - Home near the station. Alone, deliberately.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Sunday lunch with my parents.
    - Typing course. Numbers confuse me.
    - My husband's birthday, with his family.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Picking my children up from school.
    - Ask anything. I have nothing to hide.
    - Back to my village. Never lived here.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Home to my family. Mother's waiting up.
    - Settling Father's estate with my brothers.
    - Opening my flat to evacuated families.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Don't mind the mask. Old scars. Nothing interesting.
    - You have a very serious expression. I find that attractive.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Still the same face at this window. I appreciate consistency.
    - I can make this quick. We both have long days ahead.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - These last few days, I find myself almost sentimental.
    - I won't ask about your rules. You don't ask about mine.
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - My papers are ready. I was here yesterday. Remember?
    - The mask is part of my face. It stays.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I have everything you need. You can ask me things.
    - I came prepared. I always come prepared for you.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I know what you need to see. Look closer.
    - The mask does not come off. You already know why.
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Good instincts, officer. I will remember that.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - You make this easier every time. I appreciate that.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Smooth as always. Until the next one.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays: []
    dialoguesMidDays: []
    dialoguesFinalDays: []
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays: []
    dialoguesMidDays: []
    dialoguesFinalDays: []
  quarantineExitLines:
  - I will need to contact someone. One moment.
  - You will hear from people I know. I say that calmly.
  killExitLines:
  - "The mask\u2026 stays on\u2026 even now\u2026"
  - "You could have\u2026 just looked away\u2026"
